Description: fix FTBFS against glibc that defines SYS_SECCOMP as an enum
 Newer glibc (Ubuntu 26.04 "resolute") declares SYS_SECCOMP as an enum
 constant in <bits/siginfo-consts.h>, with a self-referential #define
 following it. The fallback "#define SYS_SECCOMP 1" in sandbox.h poisons
 that enum declaration when <signal.h> is included later in the same
 translation unit:
 .
   sandbox.h:24:21: error: expected identifier before numeric constant
   sandbox.c:2149:24: error: 'SYS_SECCOMP' undeclared
 .
 Include <signal.h> before the fallback so the system definition, when
 present, wins. The fallback remains for platforms without SYS_SECCOMP.
 Carried as a debian patch rather than a source change to keep the tree
 clean for upstream tor merges; drop this patch once upstream fixes it.
Author: Jim Toth <jim@memeticblock.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-07-16
--- a/src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.h
+++ b/src/lib/sandbox/sandbox.h
@@ -15,6 +15,10 @@
 #include "orconfig.h"
 #include "lib/cc/torint.h"

+#ifdef __linux__
+#include <signal.h>
+#endif
+
 #ifndef SYS_SECCOMP

 /**
